SwiftPutty local patch 0017
Upstream: PuTTY 0.85 (a3cce3a48d4ab12e0fccb32998b9042d4f7c3ff1)
Status:   not yet reported upstream; should be, PRIVATELY (a server can
          abort the client before its host key is checked)

EdDSA: reject a point encoding that is not exactly fieldBytes long.

eddsa_decode() turned the encoded point into an mp_int sized by its
length, then cleared bit fieldBytes*8-1, which mp_set_bit asserts is
within the number. An Ed25519 or Ed448 public key whose point string is
too short therefore failed that assertion (PuTTY keeps assertions in
release builds) and aborted the program. Public keys are decoded from
untrusted input in several places, among them the server's host key
during key exchange (kex2-client.c), before it is verified: a server
could end the client. In SwiftPutty, where every session shares one
process, it would end all of them.

Found by fuzzing (Core/tests/fuzz/fuzz_parsers.c, through the host CA
key parser).

--- a/crypto/ecc-ssh.c
+++ b/crypto/ecc-ssh.c
@@ -526,6 +526,13 @@
 {
     assert(curve->type == EC_EDWARDS);
 
+    /* RFC 8032 encodes a point in exactly fieldBytes bytes. A shorter
+     * string would make an mp_int too small for the mp_set_bit below
+     * (an assertion failure, so a server could end the client with
+     * its host key); a longer one is not a valid encoding either. */
+    if (encoded.len != curve->fieldBytes)
+        return NULL;
+
     mp_int *y = mp_from_bytes_le(encoded);
 
     /* The topmost bit of the encoding isn't part of y, so it stores
